                        "type": "comment",
                        "level": 4,
                        "id": "c-ExampleEditor-20260926235300-ExampleEditor-20260926193900",
                        "replies": [
                          {
                            "timestamp": "2026-09-29T00:40:00Z",
                            "author": "REDACTED",
                            "type": "comment",
                            "level": 5,
                            "id": "c-ExampleEditor-20260929004000-ExampleEditor-20260926235300",
                            "replies": [],
                            "html": "This is the English Wikipedia, used worldwide. It is not a department of the U.S. government. It should use the world's terminology. ---- <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./User:ExampleEditor\" title=\"User:ExampleEditor\" id=\"mwApY\">ExampleEditor</a> (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./User_talk:ExampleEditor\" title=\"User talk:ExampleEditor\" id=\"mwApc\">talk</a>) 00:40, 29 September 2026 (UTC)"
                          }
                        ],
                        "html": "I think that can all be safely ignored, especially there already is a concept of Super Intelligence. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./User:ExampleEditor\" title=\"User:ExampleEditor\" id=\"mwAow\">ExampleEditor</a> (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./User_talk:ExampleEditor\" title=\"User talk:ExampleEditor\" id=\"mwAo0\">talk</a>) 23:53, 26 September 2026 (UTC)"
                      }
                    ],
                    "html": "According to Trump, he and the President of China <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./Xi_Jinping\" title=\"Xi Jinping\" id=\"mwAoY\">Xi Jinping</a> agreed to refer to AI as \"super intelligence\" or \"SI\". However, the news media continues to refer to it as \"AI\".<a rel=\"mw:ExtLink nofollow\" href=\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2026/09/26/trump-xi-ai-technology-china-us/91957387007/\" class=\"external autonumber\" id=\"mwAoc\"></a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./User:ExampleEditor\" title=\"User:ExampleEditor\" id=\"mwAog\">ExampleEditor</a> (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./User_talk:ExampleEditor\" title=\"User talk:ExampleEditor\" id=\"mwAok\">talk</a>) 19:39, 26 September 2026 (UTC)"
                  }
                ],
                "html": "The <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./U.S._State_Department\" title=\"U.S. State Department\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAn4\">U.S. State Department</a> ordered its international diplomats to use \"Super Intelligence\" (\"SI\") instead of AI.<a rel=\"mw:ExtLink nofollow\" href=\"https://apnews.com/article/trump-super-intelligence-rebrand-ai-diplomats-02123c7bf18c692a12b2b3e3b9ce30c5\" class=\"external autonumber\" id=\"mwAn8\"></a> However, per <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./Wikipedia:NAMECHANGE\" title=\"Wikipedia:NAMECHANGE\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAoA\">Wikipedia's article naming policy</a>, this article should not be renamed unless an alternative name becomes prevalent in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./Wikipedia:Reliable_sources\" title=\"Wikipedia:Reliable sources\" id=\"mwAoE\">reliable sources</a>. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./User:ExampleEditor\" title=\"User:ExampleEditor\" id=\"mwAoI\">ExampleEditor</a> (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./User_talk:ExampleEditor\" title=\"User talk:ExampleEditor\" id=\"mwAoM\">talk</a>) 23:45, 24 September 2026 (UTC)"
              }
            ],
            "html": "After the UN speech by Trump, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./User:ExampleEditor\" title=\"User:ExampleEditor\" id=\"mwAm0\">User:ExampleEditor</a> first immediately moved this page to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./Super_intelligence_(SI)\" title=\"Super intelligence (SI)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAm4\">Super intelligence (SI)</a>, and when this was reverted repeatedly added 4K of prose about this to the article<a rel=\"mw:ExtLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Artificial_intelligence&amp;diff=prev&amp;oldid=1376179997\" class=\"external autonumber\" id=\"mwAm8\"></a>. While this may warrant one or two sentences in this article at most, in the end how Trump wants to call AI is not important for an encyclopedic article about the large subject AI with its long history. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./User:ExampleEditor\" title=\"User:ExampleEditor\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAnA\">ExampleEditor</a> (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./User_talk:ExampleEditor\" title=\"User talk:ExampleEditor\" id=\"mwAnE\">talk</a>) 16:08, 22 September 2026 (UTC)"
          }
        ],
